{"id":"84b11306-2c36-4495-9c06-4e4f00474d4a","object":"chat.completion","created":1785031931,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    # Extract required fields\\n    word_token_indices = case['word_token_indices']\\n    word_labels = case['word_labels']\\n    token_count = case['token_count']\\n\\n    # Validate word count\\n    if len(word_token_indices) != len(word_labels):\\n        raise ValueError('Mismatch between number of word groups and word labels')\\n\\n    # Build seen set and validate no overlap, out-of-range, and coverage\\n    seen = set()\\n    for indices in word_token_indices:\\n        for idx in indices:\\n            if idx < 0 or idx >= token_count:\\n                raise ValueError(f'Token index {idx} out of range [0, {token_count-1}]')\\n            if idx in seen:\\n                raise ValueError(f'Duplicate token index {idx}')\\n            seen.add(idx)\\n\\n    if len(seen) != token_count:\\n        raise ValueError(f'Not all tokens covered: {len(seen)} seen, expected {token_count}')\\n\\n    # Broadcast word labels to token_labels\\n    token_labels = [0] * token_count\\n    for i, indices in enumerate(word_token_indices):\\n        label = word_labels[i]\\n        for idx in indices:\\n            token_labels[idx] = label\\n\\n    # Compute kept_indices (ascending order automatically from enumeration)\\n    kept_indices = [idx for idx, lbl in enumerate(token_labels) if lbl == 1]\\n\\n    return {\\n        'kept_indices': kept_indices,\\n        'token_labels': token_labels\\n    }\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) according to the problem description. The task is NLP-LL2-01. Given a case payload with word_token_indices, word_labels, token_count, we must project word-level labels onto each token. Each word is a group of token indices (list of ints). The word_labels indicate which words to keep (1) or drop (0). For each word, we broadcast its label to all tokens in that word's group. Then we need to produce a token_labels list of length token_count, where each token gets the label from the word it belongs to. Then kept_indices are the indices (integers) where token_labels is 1, in ascending order. Must ensure alignment is complete: every token index from 0 to token_count-1 must appear exactly once across all word groups? The problem says \"Reject overlapping, out-of-range, or uncovered token indices.\" So we need to validate that the word_token_indices are a partition of the range [0, token_count-1] (no overlap, no gaps, no out-of-range). Also each word must have at least one token? Probably yes. Also there must be exactly one word label per word (word_labels length equals number of words). If any violation, raise ValueError.\n\nReturn dict with \"kept_indices\" (list of ints) and \"token_labels\" (list of ints of length token_count). The input case is the payload object. We must not mutate case.\n\nImplementation: iterate through word_token_indices, for each word index i, get its indices list and label word_labels[i]. Check that all indices are within [0, token_count-1]. Also ensure no overlap: maintain a set of seen indices, add each index from each word; if duplicate, ValueError. After processing all words, check that total seen indices equals token_count. If not (some missing), ValueError.\n\nThen create token_labels as list of length token_count initialized to 0. For each word i, for each index in word_token_indices[i], set token_labels[index] = word_labels[i] (must be 0 or 1? Probably integer 0/1). Then compute kept_indices = [idx for idx, label in enumerate(token_labels) if label == 1].\n\nReturn dict with those fields.\n\nEdge cases: token_count could be 0? Possibly but then word_token_indices should be empty list. Handle gracefully.\n\nImplement solve(case) function that returns dict.\n\nNow output as JSON with key \"implementation\" containing Python source as JSON string. Need to escape properly.\n\nWrite code. Use only standard library.\n\nAlso note: The input payload may have \"_case_nonce\" but ignore.\n\nLet's produce final answer."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1258,"completion_tokens":927,"total_tokens":2185,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1152},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":565},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1152,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":106},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}